# I03.var08 prospective contract v1: NO_GO_CONTRACT_DESIGN

The frozen prospective contract `tmp/i03-var08-prospective-contract-design-v1-20261008.json` is 104,942 bytes, SHA-256 `a9ad55703a87178751e22ed0b1bef0cba3566699a401d3201fc431909e41a9f2`. Its generator is 14,157 bytes, SHA-256 `a3a44cef8829561a8cd170d562d016d90b27b06a3ffe422b32cc73f5d6a5547d`.

The proposed ResourceTransfer columns omit `key: true` on STFID, STTID, RID, and TFTIME. The installed dictionary marks those four fields as Index fields (physical lines 682–685). Accepted I03 ResourceTransfer input represents each with `key: true`. The v1 contract also fails to fix the new table's position among the source tables. Whole metadata and table order are required source and roundtrip gates, so a later implementation could satisfy v1 while using a different model schema.

This is a contract design rejection only. No I03.var08 package, source input, SSH preflight, or native run has been constructed or performed. The parent C08 exact-limit run-02 and its original bytes remain unchanged. Review a separately versioned contract with exact column flags and insertion position; preserve v1 and this decision as historical evidence.
